{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_emhehavpwbtnwp63jho25qxqf2s6dr6tuh5dbnobfbhvnbszlgeq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **One real bug found and fixed.**\n\n## The bug\n`printHexCharLine`/`driver` are `void f(char)`. GCC's prologue re-narrows the argument register (`mov %al,mem` + `movsbl mem,%eax`), so the C callee ignores bits 8–31. Rust's `extern \"C\" fn(c_char)` lowers the param with LLVM's `signext i8` attribute, which lets an **optimised** build assume the caller already sign-extended and forward `%edi` unchanged:\n\n```\nprintHexCharLine(128i32):  C -> \"ffffff80\\n\"   Rust(release) -> \"80\\n\"\n```\n\nDebug builds truncated incidentally, so this was **release-only** — invisible to a `cargo test` run. Fix: both exports take `c_int` and narrow explicitly (`as u8 as c_char`). Release codegen is now byte-level (`inc %dil` / `movsbl %dil,%esi`), matching GCC.\n\n## Artifacts (`translation/`)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | 2 symbols (`driver`, `printHexCharLine`); C↔Rust diff empty; 0 non-libc undefined; `CMakeLists.txt` builds only `driver.c`, so nothing was left untranslated |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 11 rows, all `[x]`. C has **zero** branches/returns/asserts/pointers, so the surface is the ABI: domain extremes, one-past-range, over-wide `int` |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 26 rows, all `[x]` — both entry points incl. the undeclared low-level `printHexCharLine`, exhaustive 256-value sweeps, sign/pad/overflow boundaries, over-wide ints, interleaving, buffering |\n| `run_all.sh` | Builds C `.so`, enumerates feature combos from `Cargo.toml`, runs all phases × {debug, release}, diffs `nm -D` |\n\n## Tests (41, all via `libloading` on both `.so`s — never direct Rust calls)\n`phase_b_valid.rs` 26 · `phase_c_errors.rs` 12 · `phase_d_symbols.rs` 3. stdout compared byte-for-byte by redirecting fd 1 with `dup2` and flushing both libc stdio *and* Rust's buffer.\n\n## Gates\n- [x] `nm -D` diff empty, 0 non-libc undefined (both profiles)\n- [x] All 26 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass across randomized (fixed-seed) inputs\n- [x] All 11 `ERRORS.md` rows have passing differential tests\n- [x] No binary target on either side (C: `add_library` only; Rust: `cdylib` only) — stdout gate covered by in-process capture\n- [x] Passes under every feature combo (`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`, so default ≡ `--no-default-features`) × debug/release\n\nTwo harness pitfalls also fixed: libtest's concurrent progress output polluted captures (→ `.cargo/config.toml` sets `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1`), and `cargo test` never refreshes the `cdylib`, so the harness was loading a **stale** `.so` — it now always rebuilds into `target/ffi-so`. That stale artifact was masking the release bug.\n\nHarness validated by mutation: `%02x`→`%2x`, sign→zero extension, `wrapping_add`→`saturating_add`, symbol rename, and reverting the `c_int` fix were each caught (`lib.rs` restored afterward; `c_src/` untouched)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":228,"cache_read_input_tokens":91693,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":228,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9819a0ee-c011-4c14-82f5-3189805c26eb","uuid":"3cbba9a7-9848-44a0-8f30-69fdb402fe1f","timestamp":"2026-09-05T03:16:23.987Z"}
